{"title":"1957 AHSME Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The area of a circle inscribed in an equilateral triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/4/ee4d0c6dfd9cd55e4debe07271185a51323858a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />. The perimeter of this triangle is: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/9/23994bd3f17da9cd35fb49831cccb5e19cc3434e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 72\\sqrt{3} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 48\\sqrt{3}\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 36\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 24\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 72$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"442\" height=\"21\" />   \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/4/104af9dce61eb4c467e4ae03dc64a9d78c07c8bc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((-3,-sqrt(3))--(3,-sqrt(3))--(0,2sqrt(3))--cycle); draw(circle((0,0),sqrt(3))); dot((0,0)); draw((0,0)--(0,-sqrt(3))); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"218\" />\nWe can see that the radius of the circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/b/a9bddfa0dd561449e70720e765113a3c75dc6382.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"21\" />. We know that the radius is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of each median line of the triangle; each median line is therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c1723df91fa4d618319811d633cbd6391341412a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />. Since the median line completes a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcfee7bd8a5e15e5f6b7881c138de43651572a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> triangle, we can conclude that one of the sides of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Triple the side length and we get our answer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa8422bd58c6275b8449489f356eca1383c77cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}72}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"59\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME\" title=\"1957 AHSME\">1957 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1957 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1957 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1957\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1957 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1957 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1957 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1957 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1957 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1957 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1957 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1957 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1957 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1957 AHSME Prob